-- title:
--   U is not fixed by the branch-exchange involution
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and suppose that the quotient ring $W/(\pi)$ is nontrivial, i.e. that $\pi$ does not generate the unit ideal. Consider the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$, namely the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, together with the ring automorphism `crossingSwap` $\pi$ of this quotient induced by the coordinate-interchanging automorphism `uvSwapEquiv` of the power series ring (which carries the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal` $W$ $\pi$ to itself), and with `fixedSubring` $\pi$ the subring of elements on which `crossingSwap` $\pi$ agrees with the identity. The assertion is that the element `U` $\pi$ of the crossing model does not belong to `fixedSubring` $\pi$; that is, `U` $\pi$ is not fixed by the branch-exchange involution. Its image under `crossingSwap` $\pi$ is the element `V` $\pi$, and the hypothesis on $W/(\pi)$ is what makes these two elements distinct.
--
--   In the geometric picture this says that the first branch coordinate of the crossing local model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ is not invariant under the involution exchanging the two branches, so the invariant subring is proper. It is used in the construction of the normal form of an invariant element as a sum of an invariant expression and a multiple of `U` $\pi$, and in the corresponding statement for power series under the coordinate swap.
